<title>USA: Clinton urges AMR, pilots to reach agreement.</title>
<headline>Clinton urges AMR, pilots to reach agreement.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton Wednesday urged AMR Corp.'s American Airlines and its pilots to use the current federal mediation process to avert a possible strike.</p>
<p>&quot;I have been following it very closely,&quot; Clinton told reporters at an unrelated White House event. &quot;Today I want to say that the time has not expired, and I want to encourage parties to make maximum use of the mediation board process. That's what ought to be done today.&quot;</p>
</text>
